<title>JAPAN: Final results of Japan's Lower House election.</title>
<headline>Final results of Japan's Lower House election.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the final party-by-party result in Sunday's general elections for the Lower House of Japan's parliament, according to the Central Election Commission:</p>
<p> PARTY.............Total.......Outgoing</p>
<p> LDP................239..........211</p>
<p> Shinshinto.........156..........160</p>
<p> Democrats...........52...........52</p>
<p> Social Democrats....15...........30</p>
<p> Communists..........26...........15</p>
<p> Sakigake.............2............9</p>
<p> Minor/independents..10...........16</p>
<p> Vacant ..........................18</p>
<p>-----------------------------------</p>
<p> Total..............500..........511</p>
<p>==================================</p>
<p>(Note: New Lower House has 500 seats)</p>
</text>
